From 4605573a32b92d74afc528ddba2bcd5a6e655fbd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mkinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:54:51 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(2d): continue whole-model 2D Contour across lower
 outlines

Whole-model 2D Contour previously sectioned the part once at Top Z and let
contour_depth::ladder stop any ring where the part widened below Top Z
(such as a chamfered top island, shoulder, or closed slot floor), dropping
lower depths and tabs without failing.

Extract shared single-band helpers in machining2d::contour and add multi-band
continuation in machining2d::contour_whole (contour_whole_bodies and
contour_whole_bodies_with). Whenever a whole-model Side::Outside contour
stops early on an outer loop or opens an inner counterbore loop below Top Z,
trim the upper band, slice the overhead silhouette at the next remaining Z,
re-apply boundary controls, and continue to Bottom Z. Refuse unsliceable or
collapsed continuation planes by name with ghost moves instead of emitting a
partial toolpath.

Fixes #2436
